ementation planning, and &amp; testing and evaluation. The course also provides an applied introduction to a variety of areas that are commonly a part of Systems Engineering including creating effective project teams, customer needs evaluation, mathematical tools for system analysis, control &amp; optimization, risk analysis and mitigation, decision making strategies, project organization &amp; management, and the system life cycle. The course requires students to combine their work in this course with an outside-of-course MEng project.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring, Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: Systems Engineering distance learning students.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "EN", "lastTermsOffered": "2025SU, 2024SU, 2023SU, 2022SU", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}]}, "message": null, "meta": {"copyright": "Cornell University, Office of the University Registrar", "rosterDttm": "2025-10-15T19:07:41-0400", "catalogDttm": "2025-07-09T19:07:04-0400"}}